Machines which don't perform any form of user authorization should not
be permitted to post news articles.  In the NNTP access control file, it is
possible to specify that a machine can read news articles but not post
articles.

Forcing users to login to a Unix machine to post a message won't eliminate
the opportunity to forge messages, but it would make it more difficult which
would likely cut down on the number of forgeries.

