I think this very problem of using a Mac/PC with a fake
username/mailname is exactly the reason why we have Computer Center
personel in charge of the INTERNET connection.  For example, if you
believed a forged/fake post originated from Haverford, you would do a
whois HAVERFORD.EDU, and mail the director of Academic Computing your
commplaint.  They would take the matter from there, attempting to track
the person down.  Ultimately, they may not find the person, but they can
make it an extremely hostile environment to try to forge things in.

Also, the whole net community should encourage makers of PC and Mac
netnews software to build some kind of authenticating Newsreaders that
would require passwords from INN.  Thus only authenticated users could
access your news server.

This would offer another useful degree of security.

