Our campus policy on free speech vs harassment revolves around
whether the speaking was done in a public forum (where it would
be declared free speech and most anything goes) vs a private forum
where preventing people from holding a meeting could be viewed
as harassment.

Now here is the question is an IRC channel a public forum or
a private meeting?  I can give a fictional example to illustrate: 

A channel named the pro-choice channel is created and an anti-abortionist
essentially comes in and makes it unusable by generating so much
traffic and hate talk that all the particpants leave.

Did the anti-abortionist disrupt a private meeting or exercise his
right of free speech?

If this happened on usenet in an unmoderated list we would say tough
luck free speech.  It couldn't happen on a moderated list (except to the
moderator which is another issue).  But since a channel can be controlled
somewhat and you could make the case that this intrudee was not an
invited guest.


