>The question is more akin to "can the university limit expression
>on campus by anybody who drives in from anywhere and appropriates
>a university resource (disk space) in the process"

But the real question is: "How can a university do this in a way that's
consistent with the freedom-of-inquiry and freedom -of-thought missions of
universities?" Private universities are, of course, not bound by the First
Amendment, but they are bound by traditions that predate the First
Amendment, and those traditions are, I think, best honored by limiting
any censorship of Usenet based on content.


